id: pm-3os5p6
title: "pm health advises pm history-repair for history_drift_missing_stream, but history-repair refuses a stream with no entries"
description: "When an item's history stream is missing, pm health reports history_drift_missing_stream with the remedy pm history-repair <id>, rewritten to pm history-repair --all when several streams drift. history-repair cannot rebuild a missing stream: the --all row fails with 'No history entries exist for <id>; nothing to repair.' and the command exits 1. Found on PR #1762 while running the advised remedies on a mixed-drift fixture (one chain mismatch, one missing stream) in tests/integration/lifecycle/history-bridge.integration.spec.ts. The remedy registry entry lives in src/core/diagnostics/remediation.ts, and the bulk rewrite lives in rewriteBulkHealthRemediation in src/sdk/governance/health.ts. The fix names a command that actually rebuilds or records the missing stream, for example a baseline-reseed step, or a restore when an item can be rebuilt from history; it must also keep the bulk rewrite from advising --all for a code that --all cannot repair."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[4]: health,history,remediation,ux
created_at: "2026-11-21T07:24:50.200Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-21T15:39:30.416Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-21T15:00:04.137Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-21T15:00:04.137Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "An integration spec runs the remedy pm health names for a missing stream, per item and in bulk, and the history_drift check is ok afterwards"
parent: pm-o2kc
risk: low
confidence: 85
resolution: "history-repair rebuilds a live item's absent or record-less stream with one sealed history_repair baseline, appending to verified bytes or publishing an absent stream complete; health previews both repairs and reports history_drift_chain_unbridgeable or history_drift_unrepairable_stream with details.repair_refusals; unreadable streams get the salvage preview; bulk remedies apply only where they repair every stream (unreadable, unrepairable, version-skewed and receipt-attributed streams keep remedies per item); damaged and newer-format seals refuse typed; linked stream entries refuse at planning and are never advised a rebuild. Delivered on PR #1763 after seven Codex rounds plus Greptile and CodeRabbit; exotic-filesystem residuals filed as pm-ue6pqv."
expected_result: "Every remedy pm health names for history drift, per item and in bulk, runs to a clean history_drift check, and a stream no repair can keep is never advised a repair"
actual_result: "tests/integration/lifecycle/history-remedies.integration.spec.ts runs each advised remedy for missing, empty, absent, linked, bridgeable, unbridgeable, unrepairable, unreadable, scalar-only and receipt-attributed drift and reaches a clean history_drift check; the related suites (1630 tests) and every changed hunk's coverage pass locally"
dependencies[2]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
