close_reason: "Every history-drift remedy pm health advises repairs the streams it names, per item and in bulk"
contract_change:
  api: pm health history_drift warnings and remediation_map; pm history-repair on a record-less stream
  before: "A missing stream was advised pm history-repair <id>, which refused with nothing to repair. Every chain break was history_drift_chain_mismatch with the append-only remedy, even when the bridge or both repairs refuse. The unreadable-stream remedy was the rewriting repair. A sealed record edited without a reseal crashed the rewriting repair with unknown_error"
  after: "history-repair rebuilds a live item record-less stream with one sealed baseline (result.reseed). Health previews the repairs and reports history_drift_chain_unbridgeable (pm history-repair <id>) or history_drift_unrepairable_stream (pm history <id> --verify --full), with details.repair_refusals. The unreadable-stream remedy is the salvage preview. Bulk remedies apply only where they repair every stream. The rewriting repair refuses a damaged seal with history_record_integrity_invalid and a newer seal format with history_record_version_unsupported"
  migrate: "Callers that matched history_drift_chain_mismatch for every chain break also match history_drift_chain_unbridgeable and history_drift_unrepairable_stream, and read details.repair_refusals for the reason; counts.chain_mismatches still counts every stream whose chain fails verification"
escape_class: production_defect
gate_evidence:
  disposition: gate_added
  owner: pm-3os5p6
  gate_id: history-remedy-convergence
  negative_control: "tests/integration/lifecycle/history-remedies.integration.spec.ts runs every remedy pm health advises, per item and in bulk, for missing, empty, absent and linked streams, bridgeable and unbridgeable breaks, damaged and newer-format seals, unreadable and scalar-only streams, and receipt-attributed drift. It requires a clean history_drift check after each advised repair, and asserts that a stream no repair can keep is never given a repair remedy. tests/unit/sdk/governance/history-drift-remedies.spec.ts fixes the classification and the bulk-blocking rules, and the reseed specs prove that an absent stream is published complete or refused typed."
  local_checks[1]: node scripts/run-tests.mjs test -- tests/integration/lifecycle/history-remedies.integration.spec.ts tests/unit/sdk/governance/history-drift-remedies.spec.ts tests/unit/sdk/history tests/unit/core/fs tests/unit/commands/governance/health-command.spec.ts tests/integration/merge-receipt-health-classification.integration.spec.ts
  hosted_checks[2]: CI / Gates (static),CI / Gates (coverage)
